<title>HONG KONG: Yunnan Airlines orders two 737s - Boeing.</title>
<headline>Yunnan Airlines orders two 737s - Boeing.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boeing Corp said on Monday China's Yunnan Airlines had ordered two 737-300 aircraft for US$68 million.  </p>
<p>The two 737-300s will be powered by CFM56-3 engines from CFM International and will be delivered later this year, Boeing said in a statement.</p>
<p>French-based CFM is a joint venture between France's Snecma and General Electric Co of the US.</p>
<p>Yunnan Airlines links major Chinese cities and will start service to Bangkok and Singapore within the next few weeks, it said.</p>
<p>The Chinese airline already has 10 Boeing 737s and two 767-300s, it said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
